# The .ko-agent-sandbox/egress/rule of a project that admits its model provider and nothing
# else — the lockdown for a project whose dependency names, or hosts read, are themselves
# secrets. Under --egress=deny-unless-allowed, the default: `deny defaults` takes the defaults,
# not the public HTTPS that allow-unless-denied admits ambiently, so under that profile this file
# narrows nothing. Nothing built in survives: no forge, no registry, no documentation site. The
# agent builds only from what the project directory and the image already hold, and every
# refusal is a line in the proxy log. Change the group to the agent launched: openai for codex,
# google for agy, github for copilot.
deny defaults
allow model-provider anthropic
